s of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 9 grids runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them. In 2025, November to December came in at 39% of normal on the middle, and September to October at 70%. In 2026 so far, January to February came in at 51% of normal on the middle and February to March at 56%. Grid 17547 had its driest year in 2005 at 62% of normal.</p>"}
